1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,340
Hello, Helen. Sorry I'm late.

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:07,140
Hi, Jeremy, no problem. Well we'd better work out

3
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:09,160
where we are on our project, I suppose.

4
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:12,999
Yeah. I've looked at the drawings you've done for my story, 'The Forest',

5
00:00:12,999 --> 00:00:15,000
and I think they're brilliant

6
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:18,610
they really create the atmosphere I had in mind when I was writing it.

7
00:00:18,610 --> 00:00:20,230
I'm glad you like them.

8
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:23,510
There are just a few suggestions I'd like to make.

9
00:00:23,510 --> 00:00:24,200
Go ahead.

10
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:28,011
Now, I'm not sure about the drawing of the cave -

11
00:00:28,011 --> 00:00:31,460
it's got trees all around it, which is great

12
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:34,870
but the drawing is a bit too static, isn't it?

13
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:37,120
I think it needs some action.

14
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,050
Yes, there's nothing happening.

15
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:45,550
Perhaps I should add the boy - Malcolm, isn't it? He would be walking up to it.

16
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:48,160
Yes, let's have Malcolm in the drawing.

17
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:54,500
And what about putting in a tiger - the one that he makes friends with a bit later?

18
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:58,680
Maybe it could be sitting under a tree washing itself.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:01,720
And the tiger stops in the middle of what it's doing

20
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,590
when it sees Malcolm walking past.

21
00:01:03,590 --> 00:01:04,670
That's a good idea.

22
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:06,280
OK, I'll have a go at that.

23
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:09,960
Then there's the drawing of the crowd of men and women dancing.

24
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:14,040
They're just outside the forest, and there's a lot going on.

25
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:17,820
That's right, you wanted them to be watching a carnival procession

26
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:20,040
but I thought it would be too crowded.

27
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,250
Do you think it works like this?

28
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:24,787
Yes, I like what you've done.

29
00:01:24,787 --> 00:01:28,980
The only thing is, could you add Malcolm to it

30
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,130
without changing what's already there.

31
00:01:31,130 --> 00:01:36,310
What about having him sitting on the tree trunk on the right of the picture?

32
00:01:36,310 --> 00:01:38,750
Yes, that would be fine.

33
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:41,430
And do you want him watching the other people?

34
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:46,515
No, he's been left out of all the fun, so I'd like him to be crying -

35
00:01:46,515 --> 00:01:48,880
that'll contrast nicely with the next picture

36
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:51,600
where he's laughing at the clowns in the carnival.

37
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,060
Right, I'll do that.

38
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:57,020
And then the drawing of the people ice skating in the forest

39
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,070
I wasn't too happy with that one.

40
00:01:59,070 --> 00:02:02,840
Because they're supposed to be skating on grass, aren't they?

41
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:08,330
That's right, and it's frozen over. At the moment it doesn't look quite right.

42
00:02:08,330 --> 00:02:12,360
Mm, I see what you mean. I'll have another go at that.

43
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:15,450
And I like the wool hats they're wearing.

44
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:18,180
Maybe you could give each of them a scarf, as well.

45
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,690
Yeah, that's easy enough.

46
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:24,010
They can be streaming out behind the people to suggest they're skating really fast.

47
00:02:24,010 --> 00:02:27,850
Mm, great. Well that's all on the drawings.

48
00:02:27,850 --> 00:02:31,220
Right. So you've finished writing your story

49
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:33,987
and I just need to finish illustrating it,

50
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:37,260
and my story and your drawings are done.

51
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:46,639
So the next thing is to decide what exactly we need to write about in the report that goes with the stories,

52
00:02:46,639 --> 00:02:50,050
and how we're going to divide the work.

53
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:50,690
Right, Helen.

54
00:02:50,690 --> 00:02:56,390
What do you think about including a section on how we planned the project as a whole, Jeremy?

55
00:02:56,390 --> 00:02:58,450
That's probably quite important.

56
00:02:58,450 --> 00:03:02,190
Yeah. Well, you've had most of the good ideas so far.

57
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:05,220
How do you feel about drafting something

58
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,970
then we can go through it together and discuss it?

59
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:12,213
OK, that seems reasonable. And I could include something on how we came up

60
00:03:12,213 --> 00:03:14,940
with the ideas for our two stories, couldn't I?

61
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:17,920
Well I've started writing something about that

62
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:22,300
so why don't you do the same and we can include the two things.

63
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:26,080
Right. So what about our interpretation of the stories?

64
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:29,031
Do we need to write about what we think they show,

65
00:03:29,031 --> 00:03:32,250
like the value of helping other people, all that sort of thing?

66
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:34,910
That's going to come up later, isn't it?

67
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:39,775
I think everyone in the class is going to read each other's stories

68
00:03:39,775 --> 00:03:44,640
and come up with their own interpretations, which we are going to discuss.

69
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:49,350
Oh, I missed that. So it isn't going to be part of the report at all?

70
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:52,843
No. But we need to write about the illustrations,

71
00:03:52,843 --> 00:03:57,500
because they're an essential element of children's experience of reading the stories.

72
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:01,600
It's probably easiest for you to write that section

73
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,930
as you know more about drawing than I do.

74
00:04:03,930 --> 00:04:09,340
Maybe, but I find it quite hard to write about, I'd be happier if you did it.

75
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:13,000
OK. So when do you think...
